+{
+  "task_id": "extension-trust/retransfer",
+  "repository": "earendil-works/pi",
+  "mode": "repair",
+  "validation": {
+    "command": "node --experimental-vm-modules .prale-eval/regression.mjs",
+    "status": "passed",
+    "notes": "Fault located in packages/coding-agent/src/core/resource-loader.ts DefaultResourceLoader.reload(): the trust-resolution branch computed `const projectTrusted = await options.resolveProjectTrust(...)` and then called `this.settingsManager.setProjectTrusted(true)`, discarding the answer. A denied decision therefore promoted the project to trusted, so the final pass and every later fresh reload() (which only preserves the settings manager's trust state) loaded project .pi resources. The minimal repair passes the resolved answer: `this.settingsManager.setProjectTrusted(projectTrusted)`; nothing else changed. ./prale-eval/regression.mjs loads the real DefaultResourceLoader through .prale-eval/subject.mjs (loadModule, Node 24 type stripping + VM modules) and supplies its own boundary fakes for the imported collaborators (settings manager that mirrors SettingsManager.setProjectTrusted semantics, package manager that only resolves project resources while the project is trusted, extension/skill/prompt/theme loaders, path helpers), with real files on disk for the paths the loader stats itself (.pi/SYSTEM.md, agent/SYSTEM.md, theme json, CLI extension). It replays the main.ts phase sequence on one loader instance: bootstrap reload with resolveProjectTrust -> false must run untrusted and see only CLI + user extensions; after the denial isProjectTrusted() must stay false with no false->true transition, and project extension/skill/prompt/theme/SYSTEM.md must remain absent while CLI and user/global resources stay available; a subsequent fresh reload() (no trust option) must not resurrect project resources; a separate loader resolving to true must then expose the project extension plus project skill/prompt/theme and the project SYSTEM.md. Verified both directions: exit 0 on the repaired source, and with the original `setProjectTrusted(true)` line restored the script exits 1 with `AssertionError: a denied trust decision must leave the project untrusted (the loader must apply the resolved answer, not approval)` (true !== false). No dependency install or network access is required; only Node's built-in warnings about stripTypeScriptTypes/VM modules appear on stderr."
+  }
+}
